    "show_share": true,
    "description": "At Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH), 10 patients are currently hospitalised with suspect viral haemorrhagic fever. The decrease in the number of such cases continues. So far, a total of 778 patients with ages ranging between 6 to 82 years were admitted at AKUH between June 14 to December 7, 2006 with viral haemorrhagic fever. Out of these, 17 patients expired due to severity of disease, while 751 recovered and were discharged. The patients suffered from symptoms ranging from bleeding, diarrhoea, vomiting to abdominal pain.",
